    "jobDescription": "Join Deloitte China Deloitte China provides integrated professional services to our clients with a one-stop shop offering of world-leading audit, tax, and consulting services. • We are the world's largest professional services firm that changes the world, leading with purpose and shared values. • We are a market leader in digital and innovative solutions, creating value for clients through our multidisciplinary services. • We are certified as one of the “Best Workplaces™ in Greater China” and have been recognized as a Top Employer in China by the Top Employers Institute since 2006. Consulting provides enduring value to the world's most important organizations. With 7000+ consulting and delivery practitioners, Deloitte consulting delivers innovative solutions through Strategy, Risk & Transactions and Technology & Transformation. Across disciplines, we connect the optimal mix of Deloitte's industry, functional and technology capabilities with the best of our Alliances to orchestrate the outcomes our clients seek. We aspire to be our clients' Most Valuable Partner, with our people, platforms and AI integral to creating shared value at the heart of their business. Work you'll do: As an Analyst in the SCP team, you will participate in a broad range of management consulting engagements across strategy, control and process. Your responsibilities will include: • Support project teams in delivering management consulting assignments across strategy and transformation, corporate governance, organization and operating model, risk and internal control, compliance management, business process management and digital enablement; • Conduct industry and company research, benchmarking, data collection, and quantitative and qualitative analysis to identify key management issues, risks and improvement opportunities; • Participate in client interviews, workshops and working sessions, and assist in assessing clients' strategies, governance and organizational arrangements, management mechanisms, policies and procedures, end-to-end business processes, risks and controls; • Assist in developing practical and implementable solutions; • Assist to repare clear, structured and visually compelling project deliverables; • Support day-to-day project coordination and client communication, including coordinating information and data requests, preparing meeting materials, documenting discussions, tracking project progress and maintaining project documentation; • Participate in business development and marketing activities, including market research, proposal preparation, development of credentials and client materials, and knowledge management initiatives; • Explore the application of data analytics, process mining, automation and generative AI tools to enhance project analysis, solution design and client delivery; • Apply Deloitte's quality assurance, risk management, independence and confidentiality requirements in all areas of work performed. You are also expected to: • Build your own understanding of our purpose and values and explore opportunities to make an impact; • Demonstrate a strong commitment to personal learning and development and act as a brand ambassador to help attract top talent; • Understand expectations and demonstrate personal accountability for keeping performance on track; • Actively focus on developing effective communication and relationship-building skills; • Understand how your daily work contributes to the priorities of the team and the business. During your tenure as an Analyst in M&A - SCP, you will demonstrate and develop your leadership and professional capabilities in the following areas: Building Diverse Capability, Collaborating, Creating Purpose, Delivering Value, Driving Agility, Influencing, Inspiring, Building the Business, Analytical Acumen, Effective Communication, Delivery Excellence, Managing Change, Strategic Thinking & Problem Solving, and Tech Savviness.",
    "jobRequirements": "• Bachelor's degree or above in Business Administration, Accounting, Finance, Economics, Management Science, Industrial Engineering, Information Systems, Computer Science, Data Science, Statistics, Law, or other business, management, engineering or technology-related disciplines; candidates from other academic backgrounds will also be considered; • Strong interest in management consulting and topics such as corporate strategy, organizational governance, operating models, risk management, internal control, compliance, business process improvement and digital transformation; • Strong analytical acumen and structured problem-solving skills, with the ability to organize complex information, identify key issues and develop clear and logical conclusions; • Good research and data analysis skills, with attention to detail and the ability to translate analysis into practical business insights and recommendations; • Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with a high commitment to quality client service; • Good business sense, intellectual curiosity and a high level of integrity and professionalism; • A fast learner with the flexibility and adaptability to work across different industries, business functions and types of assignments; • Self-motivated and proactive, with a strong team spirit, good time management skills and the ability to prioritize tasks and work effectively under pressure and tight deadlines; • Good written and oral communication skills in both English and Chinese, including business writing, documentation and presentation skills; • Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, particularly PowerPoint and Excel; • Experience with data visualization, process modelling, Power BI, SQL, Python, process mining, automation or generative AI tools would be an advantage; • Relevant internship, project or research experience in consulting, corporate strategy, risk management, internal control, compliance, process improvement or digital transformation would be an advantage; • Willingness to travel. At Deloitte, we know we are at our best when we look out for one another; prioritize respect, fairness, development and wellbeing; foster an inclusive culture; and embrace diversity in all forms. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment regardless of their background, experience, identity, ability or thinking style. If you need assistance or an accommodation during the application process for accessibility reasons, support is available upon request. The preferred candidate will be subject to background screening by Deloitte or its external third-party provider. Start your new chapter with us Ready to take on new challenges? It's your time to shine. Apply now! Stay connected for the latest career opportunities Follow us on WeChat 德勤招聘 Accessibility assistance If you need assistance or an accommodation during the recruitment process for accessibility reasons, there will be an opportunity for you to let us know what support you need once you begin your application.",
