    "salary": "",
    "status": "推荐",
    "discoveredAt": "2026-09-10T22:12:01.908Z",
    "jobDescription": "Join Deloitte China Deloitte China provides integrated professional services to our clients with a one-stop shop offering of world-leading audit, tax, and consulting services. • We are the world's largest professional services firm that changes the world, leading with purpose and shared values. • We are market leader in digital and innovative solutions, creating value for client through our multi-disciplinary services. • We are certified as one of the ‘Best Workplaces™ in Greater China and recognized as a Top Employer in China by the Top Employers Institute* since 2006！ Consulting provides enduring value to the world's most important organizations. With 7000+ consulting and delivery practitioners, Deloitte consulting delivers innovative solutions through Strategy, Risk & Transactions and Technology & Transformation. Across disciplines, we connect the optimal mix of Deloitte's industry, functional and technology capabilities with the best of our Alliances to orchestrate the outcomes our clients seek. We aspire to be our clients' Most Valuable Partner, with our people, platforms and AI integral to creating shared value at the heart of their business. Work you will do As an Analyst within our Human Capital Organization Transformation practice, you will support leading organizations in reimagining how work gets done in an AI-enabled world. You will work alongside experienced consultants to help clients navigate workforce transformation, redesign operating models, and build future-ready capabilities that integrate human and digital talent. This role is ideal for individuals who are passionate about the intersection of people, technology, and business strategy, and who want to shape how organizations evolve in response to rapid advancements in AI and automation. Key responsibilities include: • Support the design and delivery of organization transformation and workforce strategy projects across industries • Conduct research and analysis on future-of-work trends, including AI adoption, automation, and emerging skills • Assist in developing organization and workforce transformation strategies, including job redesign, skills taxonomy, competency frameworks, target operating model design, organizational structure design, experience journey and business process design etc. • Contribute to organizational change management initiatives for large-scale transformations driven by digital, AI and other strategic agenda • Analyze workforce data (e.g., skills, productivity, capacity) to generate insights and inform strategic recommendations • Support the development of learning and upskilling programs, particularly in digital, data, and AI capabilities • Prepare client-ready deliverables including presentations, reports, and workshop materials • Collaborate with cross-functional teams to integrate human capital considerations into broader business transformation efforts What You Will Learn • How leading organizations are deploying AI and automation to transform work, workforce, and workplaces • Practical approaches to workforce planning, skills-based organization design, and talent strategy • Change management methodologies to drive adoption of new technologies and ways of working • Exposure to senior client stakeholders and complex, large-scale transformation programs During your tenure as an analyst in Organization Transformation, you will demonstrate and develop your leadership and professional capabilities in the following areas: Building diverse capability, Collaborating, Creating purpose, Delivering value, Driving agility, Influencing, Inspiring, Building the Business, Analytical Acumen, Effective Communication, Delivery Excellence, Managing Change, Strategic Thinking & Problem Solving and Tech Savviness.",
    "jobRequirements": "• Bachelor or above degree holder in Business, Human Resources, Psychology, Data Analytics, or a related field • Demonstrated interest and experiences in the following areas: future of work, digital transformation, AI, organizational development, talent strategy, organizational change management • Analytical mindset with ability to synthesize data into actionable insights • Excellent problem-solving and teamwork skills • Self-driven and willingness to work under pressure • Excellent written and oral communication skills in both English and Chinese, including consulting-style presentation, research findings and analyses • Proficiency in PowerPoint and Excel; familiarity with data analytics tools or AI platforms is an advantage • Acceptance to business travel At Deloitte, we know we’re at our best when we look out for one another; prioritize respect, fairness, development and wellbeing; foster an inclusive culture and embrace diversity in all forms. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment regardless of their background, experience, identity, ability or thinking style, and if you need assistance or an accommodation during the application process for accessibility reasons this is available upon request. The preferred candidate will be subject to background screening by Deloitte or by their external third-party provider. Start your new chapter with us Ready to take on new challenges? It's your time to shine. Apply now! Stay connected for the latest career opportunities Follow us on WeChat 德勤招聘 Accessibility assistance If you need assistance or an accommodation during the recruitment process for accessibility reasons, there will be an opportunity for you to let us know what you need once you begin your application.",
